---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="About the Translaudio project and its mission.">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16 lg:pt-32 lg:pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h1 class="heading-display text-5xl lg:text-7xl mb-6 reveal stagger-1">
          Audio deserves<br />
          <span class="italic text-copper">better tools.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-ink-muted leading-relaxed reveal stagger-2">
          We spend hours in lectures, podcasts, and meetings. The content is rich, but trapped
          in a format that's hard to search, reference, or build on. Translaudio changes that.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- Mission -->
  <section class="py-24 lg:py-32">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2 class="heading-editorial text-4xl lg:text-5xl mb-8">
            The problem<br />with audio
          </h2>
          <div class="space-y-6 text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              Audio is one of the richest sources of knowledge. Lectures explain concepts
              that textbooks can't. Conversations capture nuance that documentation misses.
              Podcasts explore ideas in depth.
            </p>
            <p>
              But audio is also one of the hardest formats to work with. You can't search it.
              You can't skim it. You can't quote it. You can't link to a specific insight
              buried 47 minutes into a recording.
            </p>
            <p>
              Translaudio exists to bridge that gap. It transforms audio from a passive,
              linear experience into a structured, queryable knowledge base &mdash; and then
              goes further by actively recommending resources to deepen your understanding.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
